menu "Robot application"
config ROBOT_CALIBRATION_GPIO
    int "Calibration button GPIO (active LOW, internal pull-up)"
    range 0 21
    default 5
    help
        Connect a normally-open button between this GPIO and GND. A stable LOW
        requests maintenance mode without reset. Enabling the integration creates
        one priority-1 polling task (2048-byte stack); no GPIO ISR is installed.
        Board integration accepts only
        unused exposed GPIOs 4, 5, 6, 20 or 21; occupied pins fail initialization.

config ROBOT_CALIBRATION_DEBOUNCE_MS
    int "Calibration button stable interval (ms)"
    range 20 1000
    default 50
    help
        Both LOW acceptance and HIGH rearming require this stable interval.
        Input polling occurs every 10 ms in a low-priority task; scheduling can
        add latency. Mode entry waits for any active controller to stop/join.

config ROBOT_CALIBRATION_LED_GPIO
    int "Optional calibration LED GPIO (-1 disables)"
    range -1 21
    default -1
    help
        Optional external LED, toggled every 250 ms while maintenance is active.
        Use a free GPIO (4, 5, 6, 20 or 21), different from the button, with a
        series resistor. The onboard GPIO8 LED shares encoder SDA and cannot
        be blinked in this integration. Default disabled adds no output pin.

config ROBOT_CALIBRATION_LED_ACTIVE_LEVEL
    int "LED active level (0 or 1)"
    range 0 1
    default 1
    help
        Electrical level that lights the optional external LED. The opposite
        level is applied during setup and while normal mode is active. This
        setting has no GPIO effect when the LED GPIO is -1; it does not permit
        using the onboard LED on the encoder SDA pin.

endmenu
